  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;&lt;span id=&quot;docs-internal-guid-a6ab5f31-7fff-3180-4007-e93e3c7848ee&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;&quot;&gt;The proposed development, by reason of insufficient supporting information, fails to demonstrate compliance with local and regional policies aimed at protecting and promoting employment floorspace. The application does not provide adequate evidence of demand, adaptability, or fit out in relation to the proposed Class Eg use. The proposal is deemed contrary to policies LP27 (Protecting and Promoting Office Floorspace in the Borough), LP28 (Protecting and Promoting Industrial Land and Floorspace in the Borough, and LP30 (Railway Arches) of the Hackney Local Plan 2033 and Policies E1 (Offices) and E4 (Land for Industry, Logistics and Services to Support London’s Economy) of the London Plan 2021.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-tab-span&quot; style=&quot;text-wrap-mode: nowrap;&quot;&gt;\t&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;&lt;span id=&quot;docs-internal-guid-ce5bb316-7fff-846a-f291-d0597880159f&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;&quot;&gt;The proposed development, by reason of a lack of sufficient and suitable information regarding the amenity impacts of the development, fails to alleviate the Council’s concerns the proposal would result in adverse noise, disturbance and odour impacts to the detriment of the living conditions of adjoining residential occupiers . The proposal is therefore deemed contrary to Policies LP2 (Development and Amenity), LP26 (Employment Land and Floorspace) and LP58 (Improving the Environment - Pollution) of the Hackney Local Plan 2033 and Policy D14 (Noise) of the London Plan 2021.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
